    {
      "text": "in the river, and they shall be turned to blood, Ex. 7:17. They have turned aside quickly out of the way, Ex. 32:8. if thou turn to the Lord, Deut. 4:30. ye shall not turn aside to the right hand, Deut. 5:32 (Prov. 4:27). turn not aside from the commandment, Deut. 17:20. shalt be turned into another man, 1 Sam. 10:6. ends of the world shall … turn unto the Lord, Ps. 22:27. Turn us again … cause thy face to shine, Ps. 80:3 (80:7, 19). Lord turned again the captivity of Zion, Ps. 126:1. soft answer turneth away wrath, Prov. 15:1. all are of the dust, and all turn to dust, Eccl. 3:20. turneth it upside down, Isa. 24:1. turn aside the just for a thing of nought, Isa. 29:21 (2 Ne. 27:32). we have turned every one to his own way, Isa. 53:6 (Mosiah 14:6). turned back to the iniquities of their forefathers, Jer. 11:10. If that nation … turn from their evil, Jer. 18:8. turn thou me, and I shall be turned, Jer. 31:18. When a righteous man doth turn from his righteousness … he shall die, Ezek. 3:20. turn yourselves from your idols, Ezek. 14:6. turn yourselves from all your transgressions, Ezek. 18:30. they that turn many to righteousness as the stars, Dan. 12:3. turn thou to thy God, Hosea 12:6. turn ye even to me with all your heart, Joel 2:12. turn every one from his evil way, Jonah 3:8. Turn ye unto me … and I will turn unto you, Zech. 1:3. turn the heart of the fathers to the children, Mal. 4:6 (Luke 1:17; 3 Ne. 25:6; D&C 27:9; 110:15; 128:17; JS—H 1:39).",
